.TH BYTEKEYSD 8 "October 2026" "ByteKeys 1.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
bytekeysd \- ByteKeys keyboard lighting, fan and power service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bytekeysd
[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-input\fR] [\fB\-\-demo\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bytekeysd
owns the keyboard lighting, performance and fan hardware. It applies the
chosen lighting, runs effects and automation rules, switches performance
modes, keeps custom fan curves active (the kernel drops them on every mode
change, at boot and after suspend), restores the battery charge limit,
reports the vendor launch key, and serves the
.BR bytekeys (1)
tools over a Unix socket. Anyone may query it; changes are accepted from
root, members of the
.B bytekeys
group and the user of the active local session.
.PP
It is normally started by systemd
.RB ( bytekeysd.service ).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Control socket (default /run/bytekeys/bytekeysd.sock).
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " DIR"
Where settings are kept (default /var/lib/bytekeys).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-input
Do not watch input devices. Disables idle rules, the Reactive effect and the
launch key. Only the time of the last input and presses of the configured
launch key are ever used, never which other keys were pressed.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Add simulated keyboards and fans (nothing is written to fans then).
.TP
.B \-v
Debug logging.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bytekeys (1),
.BR bytekeys-gui (1)
